{
  "name": "mantis",
  "_about": "A mantis -- the praying mantis (Mantis religiosa), 7 cm long: long and green; the prothorax a long neck raised up in front, carrying a small free-turning triangular head with big eyes at its corners and thin antennae; the raptorial forelegs -- long coxae, the femora armed beneath with spines, the spined tibiae folded back against them like jack-knives -- held up before the face as if in prayer; two pairs of long thin walking legs; green tegmina lying flat over a broad abdomen. On the inner face of each fore coxa a black eye-spot ringed white. Coat: brown. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
